WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Tears Abound as Disney's Unpaid Experts Are Crowned

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:15.000
"My American dream was to go to Walt Disney World," says Aena Drone, who came to the US from Pakistan as a child.

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:20.000
It's safe to say that as of now, she has long surpassed her dream.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:37.000
Why is that? The 36-year-old is one of 14 people selected from 10,000 applicants who are joining 28 returning members as the 2024 Disney Parks Moms Panel.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:46.000
This panel is a group of volunteer ‘Disney experts’ who assist travelers in planning their Disney vacations.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:56.000
To encourage honesty, none of the panelists are paid, and their workload is to answer about 15 questions a week.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:11.000
According to a press release from Disney, the panelists dedicate their free time to answering questions like where to find Disney World's private nursing rooms and all those hidden Mickeys.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:18.000
For this, each panel member gets a free, five-night stay for four people at the resort.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:27.000
These Disney superfans have a combined total of 714 Disney vacations under their belts.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:36.000
"When I was young and my parents told me that I was moving to America from Pakistan, it was scary. 

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:44.000
But they also told me Mickey Mouse lived in America because he was my hero," says Drone.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:55.000
When interviewed for this report, the stay-at-home mom of two boys became so overwhelmed that she started to cry," noted the reporter.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:08.000
Tamela Hansen of Alabama, who has visited Disney World at least 100 times, said she had applied to be a panelist 12 times before she was finally selected. 

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:17.000
Almost all of the new panelists, who serve in the year-long contractor role, said they felt they were part of the Disney family. 

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:32.000
Three of the panelists are men, two are childless, and each has their own area of expertise. Some are already hard at work answering enthusiastic Disney travelers.
